{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - Policy - Okta Policy Deactivated",
	"Description": "An Okta policy was deactivated. A deactivated policy stops being enforced without leaving an obvious gap in the policy list, which makes it a quieter way to disable a control than deleting it.\n\nEvent type: policy.lifecycle.deactivate\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_okta_attempt_to_deactivate_okta_policy/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
